    "notes": "ONE part \"Piano\" (two staves, brace). In every measure the left hand plays groups of four eighths beamed ACROSS the staves: two notes on the bass staff (stems up) and two on the treble staff (stems down) - these treble-staff notes belong to the LEFT hand (voice 5, <staff>1</staff>), not to the right-hand melody. In m.7 one right-hand note (g, stem down) is printed on the bass staff (voice 1, <staff>2</staff>)."
  },
  "notes": [
    "Cross-staff notes keep their voice and carry the staff they are printed on (<staff>)."
